            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I upped both the butter and olive oil to tablespoons. I did saute these a little longer than the recipe asked for, only because mine were not quite ready after 45 seconds. Though my family was lukewarm about this, I loved it. What my family didn't want, I happily ate for them. VERY good. Next time, I think I might throw in some chopped shallots. I think that would make this dish even tastier!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "THYMEKEEPER"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've had some Brussels sprouts sitting in the fridge and didn't want them to go to waste. I shredded them quite finely and eyeballed everything. Fried four strips of turkey bacon, removed them from the pan, added about 2 tbsp of butter, 1 tbsp of canola oil, added the Brussels sprouts and juice of one lemon. Cooked the liquid off and added the bacon back in. So good! Thank you for a great, easy recipe. I will make again.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-08T23:39:29.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "brenda boyle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added the butter and olive oil to a cast iron pan that I had just finished browning some Greek marinated chicken in. After it was deglazed I added the brussel sprouts, cooked the for about two minutes, then added the salt and pepper, squeezed half a lemon over them and tossed. OH. EM. GEE. These are SO GOOD and super easy!",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-24T01:26:30.720Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Iloveit"
            },
            "reviewBody": "LOVED IT EASY. The work is in the shredding. Once that is done, it's an easy vegetable. I use my hand mandolin. I do\na full bag of Costco Brussels sprouts and I am set for a while.\nIt keeps in fridge, but am going to try and freeze. Watch the lemon juice, necessary but doesn't need a lot. If I have on hand I will add a little bacon next time.",
            "datePublished": "2017-02-18T18:48:23.067Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jeremy H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Modified the thin slice sprouts concept to add 4-5 shallots (ring-sliced to similar thickness) and one diced apple kicked this recipe from a 4 to an easy 5.",
            "datePublished": "2018-10-24T01:13:13.853Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ms Jean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I usually do sprouts whole or half. I was surprised how easy they sliced, and I also liked how they came out. I upped the olive oil and butter to about a tblsp. The cooking time of 45 sec didn't work for me (as others mentioned, as well). I sauteed them at least 3 min, and they started to brown just a little. They were not soggy, just cooked right. New, delicious way to do sprouts!",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-24T16:19:07.273Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "crazy4cakes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe. Even my hubby who hates Brussel sprouts liked it. I omitted the lemon juice just because I didn't have any and added 6 tiny chopped pearl onions and 1/2 tsp chopped garlic. Cooked on high for about 3 minutes til they were soft. So delicious! Definitely a keeper and I'll be making this regularly!",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-08T16:35:38.747Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Crissa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were AMAZING. I usually only halve or quarter my brussels before cooking but this takes so much less time. Also, I was drinking a glass of red while cooking dinner and because I like mine a little over done, I added a splash or 3 of my wine to get some of goodness off of the pan and let it cook off. SO GOOD.",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-05T06:19:22.317Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessica Weiss Hopen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Like other reviewers, cooked longer, more like 3 min, but halved the sprouts, doubled the recipe and added a dash of red pepper flakes. Perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-11T01:13:48.613Z"
          },
          {
